WEBVTT

00:00:07.410 --> 00:00:10.870
"Higuchi Productions"

00:00:11.120 --> 00:00:15.540
I-Is that true...?

00:00:16.700 --> 00:00:19.120
Those girls...

00:00:19.120 --> 00:00:22.620
Is it the fate of SPR5 to disappear as well?

00:00:32.830 --> 00:00:36.370
No way. We're going to be disbanded?

00:00:39.540 --> 00:00:41.250
Us?

00:02:08.750 --> 00:02:12.950
"AFTERLOST"

00:02:14.080 --> 00:02:19.000
"Episode 3: Memory"

00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:21.000
"First Year Anniversary of SPR5 Concert
'One Step Toward the Other Side of Our Dream'"

00:02:23.040 --> 00:02:25.620
Yumiko! Are you okay?!

00:02:27.700 --> 00:02:31.660
Yes. How about all of you?

00:02:31.660 --> 00:02:35.580
I see. Thank goodness.

00:02:35.580 --> 00:02:39.790
I'll head toward Kouta for now.

00:02:41.160 --> 00:02:43.830
Go it. We'll meet up afterwards.

00:02:43.830 --> 00:02:47.160
We're with Geek right now.
Since we have a car...

00:03:24.830 --> 00:03:28.040
You all right? Looks like you had a bad dream.

00:03:28.040 --> 00:03:31.330
I'm fine. Just a little tired.

00:03:31.330 --> 00:03:34.870
Sleep. They say children who
sleep properly grow up healthily.

00:03:34.870 --> 00:03:36.290
Huh?

00:03:36.290 --> 00:03:38.700
Don't treat me like a kid.

00:03:43.950 --> 00:03:47.950
"First Year Anniversary of SPR5 Concert
'One Step Toward the Other Side of Our Dream'"

00:03:48.120 --> 00:03:52.290
Just like I thought! Huh? Huh?

00:03:52.290 --> 00:03:53.250
--Takuya!
--Geek!

00:03:53.250 --> 00:03:54.330
Y-Yeah.

00:03:54.330 --> 00:03:56.700
Aren't we going around in circles?

00:03:56.700 --> 00:03:59.790
Did you just see that? An SPR5 concert!

00:03:59.790 --> 00:04:01.250
There are more important...!

00:04:01.250 --> 00:04:02.620
No, something's wrong!

00:04:02.620 --> 00:04:05.700
SPR5 was caught up in Lost!

00:04:05.700 --> 00:04:07.450
I didn't know.

00:04:07.450 --> 00:04:13.290
Takuya, this may be a serious problem.

00:04:13.290 --> 00:04:14.950
What the hell is going on?

00:04:14.950 --> 00:04:17.750
What happened to us?

00:04:20.500 --> 00:04:24.540
This is bad! We're definitely trapped!

00:04:25.830 --> 00:04:31.290
Considering how we've been moving,
looks we're stuck in this general area.

00:04:31.290 --> 00:04:32.660
And this venue...

00:04:32.660 --> 00:04:37.410
...SPR5 has only done a concert here once before.

00:04:37.410 --> 00:04:42.290
Three months later, they had their concert at
the martial arts hall and got caught in Lost.

00:04:42.290 --> 00:04:44.290
What's going on?!

00:04:48.660 --> 00:04:50.080
Yua!

00:04:54.160 --> 00:04:56.250
SPR5...

00:04:56.250 --> 00:04:57.370
Wait, Yua!

00:04:57.370 --> 00:05:00.500
I'm not trying to get ahead
of everyone or anything!

00:05:00.500 --> 00:05:03.000
I just think we need to increase
the number of our fans!

00:05:03.000 --> 00:05:06.830
Mr. Seiji told us to stop
the hand-shaking events.

00:05:06.830 --> 00:05:09.080
Didn't we all agree to stop?

00:05:09.080 --> 00:05:10.120
But!

00:05:10.120 --> 00:05:12.660
We have to focus on our
performance level right now!

00:05:12.660 --> 00:05:16.330
Let's let Mr. Seiji focus on promotion.

00:05:16.330 --> 00:05:21.540
Hey, Rena, do you think things
are fine the way they are now?

00:05:21.540 --> 00:05:27.080
My hands are already full trying
to stay on the popularity poll...

00:05:28.750 --> 00:05:32.040
SPR5...

00:05:32.040 --> 00:05:35.540
Yua-<i>tan </i>is right in front of me...

00:05:35.540 --> 00:05:38.200
Looks like they're fighting amongst themselves.

00:05:38.200 --> 00:05:43.580
But, at this rate, didn't I tell you
we're going to be disbanded?!

00:05:45.410 --> 00:05:49.000
Mr. Seiji would never do something like that.

00:05:49.000 --> 00:05:51.660
Yua, the exhaustion is getting to you.

00:05:51.660 --> 00:05:53.750
Why don't you all understand?!

00:05:53.750 --> 00:05:55.040
Forget it!

00:05:55.040 --> 00:05:56.410
Yua!

00:05:57.870 --> 00:05:59.950
Geek!

00:05:59.950 --> 00:06:04.160
I know it's bothering you,
but we have to think of a way out first.

00:06:04.160 --> 00:06:04.950
But...

00:06:04.950 --> 00:06:07.370
There are routes we haven't tried yet.

00:06:09.910 --> 00:06:11.540
Fine...

00:06:20.660 --> 00:06:22.080
Kouta?

00:06:46.830 --> 00:06:47.910
Wait, Yua!

00:06:47.910 --> 00:06:51.000
I'm not trying to get ahead
of everyone or anything!

00:06:51.000 --> 00:06:54.000
--The same conversation...
--I just think we need to increase
the number of our fans!

00:06:54.000 --> 00:06:58.660
We're not only stuck in a certain area,
but in a certain time loop?

00:06:58.660 --> 00:07:00.700
Why don't you all understand?!

00:07:00.700 --> 00:07:02.000
Forget it!

00:07:02.000 --> 00:07:03.330
Yua!

00:07:11.120 --> 00:07:11.660
Sorry!

00:07:11.660 --> 00:07:12.830
Hey, Geek!

00:07:12.830 --> 00:07:14.500
Me, too.

00:07:14.500 --> 00:07:16.120
I want to go, too!

00:07:17.500 --> 00:07:19.750
Yua-<i>tan</i>!

00:07:36.580 --> 00:07:38.000
There she is!

00:07:46.040 --> 00:07:48.040
Um...

00:07:48.040 --> 00:07:49.370
Yua-<i>tan</i>.

00:07:51.000 --> 00:07:52.910
Right?

00:07:52.910 --> 00:07:53.750
Huh?

00:07:53.750 --> 00:07:58.410
The concert will start without you
if you don't hurry back?

00:07:58.410 --> 00:08:01.790
No, you have the wrong person.

00:08:01.790 --> 00:08:05.200
Well, that was a normal reaction.

00:08:05.200 --> 00:08:06.500
If I remember correctly,

00:08:06.500 --> 00:08:11.950
the concert today celebrated the first
year of the current members of SPR5.

00:08:11.950 --> 00:08:14.620
I remember it, too.

00:08:14.620 --> 00:08:18.910
It was an anniversary concert,
but only Yua didn't participate.

00:08:18.910 --> 00:08:19.830
That's right.

00:08:19.830 --> 00:08:22.620
There was an announcement
that Yua wasn't feeling well.

00:08:22.620 --> 00:08:26.830
There was a lot of controversy since
the fans didn't believe she was sick.

00:08:26.830 --> 00:08:29.620
Sorry, but we don't have time
to deal with her right now.

00:08:29.620 --> 00:08:33.450
No, Takuya. I'm sure of it now.

00:08:33.450 --> 00:08:35.620
This is the past.

00:08:35.620 --> 00:08:41.580
We probably entered a rip in space-time
because we got too close to Lost.

00:08:42.660 --> 00:08:45.450
If we change the past,
it should change the future!

00:08:45.450 --> 00:08:46.580
Sorry, Takuya!

00:08:46.580 --> 00:08:47.750
Hey!

00:08:49.160 --> 00:08:52.580
I'm going to try and save them from Lost!

00:08:54.160 --> 00:08:59.750
If that were the case, why would we
be repeating the same time loop?

00:09:02.450 --> 00:09:06.950
I'm worried about Yumiko
and Kouta. Let's go back.

00:09:09.750 --> 00:09:12.080
Yua's been acting weird lately.

00:09:12.080 --> 00:09:14.450
I wonder what happened to her?

00:09:14.450 --> 00:09:19.750
What should we do? We can't
go on stage without Yua...

00:09:19.750 --> 00:09:22.250
But we've opened the doors already...

00:09:22.250 --> 00:09:24.750
Please come back...

00:09:27.500 --> 00:09:29.000
Miss Atsuko!

00:09:29.000 --> 00:09:31.450
Listen carefully, everyone.

00:09:31.450 --> 00:09:35.290
I have a message from Mr. Seiji.

00:09:35.290 --> 00:09:36.830
Huh?

00:09:36.830 --> 00:09:39.870
But, then Yua will...

00:09:39.870 --> 00:09:42.830
We can't stop our performances on stage.

00:09:42.830 --> 00:09:46.370
We'll announce to the public
that she isn't feeling well.

00:09:48.200 --> 00:09:50.040
No way...

00:09:58.120 --> 00:10:00.750
Just like I thought!

00:10:00.750 --> 00:10:03.450
H-Huh?! How did...?

00:10:03.450 --> 00:10:07.660
You wrote that you liked
this place... on your blog!

00:10:09.120 --> 00:10:11.080
I haven't written anything like that!

00:10:11.080 --> 00:10:13.700
You will. In the future!

00:10:15.330 --> 00:10:18.410
Yua, listen to me.

00:10:18.410 --> 00:10:20.580
The concert at the
martial arts hall in three months.

00:10:20.580 --> 00:10:22.790
I want you to cancel it.

00:10:22.790 --> 00:10:25.660
Huh? What are you saying?

00:10:25.660 --> 00:10:28.410
No use, huh? Of course not.

00:10:28.410 --> 00:10:33.910
But I have to change the current
flow of things. You got this!

00:10:33.910 --> 00:10:38.200
S-Sorry, Yua. I was worried because
you haven't been doing well lately.

00:10:38.200 --> 00:10:42.410
I mean, you never messed up
on your choreography before...

00:10:44.000 --> 00:10:49.080
At this rate, I was worried about
the concert at the martial arts hall.

00:10:51.790 --> 00:10:54.700
Tama-Shi? Yua, just now?

00:10:54.700 --> 00:10:57.950
Probably. My heart is telling me so.

00:10:57.950 --> 00:11:02.540
I think she's the one who made
this weird pocket of space.

00:11:02.540 --> 00:11:04.790
What makes you think that?

00:11:05.870 --> 00:11:08.910
What in the world are Tama-Shi, anyways?

00:11:08.910 --> 00:11:11.040
They may have been humans once,

00:11:11.040 --> 00:11:15.370
but, so far, they've only been enemies
who attack without question.

00:11:15.370 --> 00:11:19.160
Someone might be controlling them...

00:11:19.160 --> 00:11:24.200
So there's someone else
who can call Tama-Shi here?

00:11:24.200 --> 00:11:25.950
I don't know.

00:11:25.950 --> 00:11:28.370
There are too many things we don't know.

00:11:28.370 --> 00:11:31.700
You awoke to your power there, didn't you?

00:11:31.700 --> 00:11:34.080
What did the Agency do to you?

00:11:36.830 --> 00:11:38.160
Sorry.

00:11:39.330 --> 00:11:40.500
Shit.

00:11:41.580 --> 00:11:44.660
We're back to where we started again.

00:11:44.660 --> 00:11:48.660
You're talking about my
last concert, right? That mistake.

00:11:48.660 --> 00:11:52.000
I messed up because I tried to
do a complicated choreography...

00:11:52.000 --> 00:11:57.160
Wasn't that because Rena wasn't
feeling well and you took her place?

00:11:59.200 --> 00:12:00.410
You have good eyes...

00:12:00.410 --> 00:12:01.500
Of course!

00:12:01.500 --> 00:12:06.580
It's easy for people to misunderstand you,
but you're a hard worker and really kind.

00:12:06.580 --> 00:12:09.290
No, no. I'm just devious on the inside.

00:12:09.290 --> 00:12:10.700
That's not true!

00:12:10.700 --> 00:12:14.700
Even that was a persona you
made to increase fans, right?

00:12:14.700 --> 00:12:16.700
Aw, I've been found out.

00:12:16.700 --> 00:12:22.040
You don't have to force yourself
to act like a little villain. Why?

00:12:22.040 --> 00:12:25.950
I know that you'd be able to take
the top in the popularity polls.

00:12:25.950 --> 00:12:30.120
You don't have to sacrifice
yourself so much for your team!

00:12:30.120 --> 00:12:35.620
You're an integral part of the
team just the way you are!

00:12:35.620 --> 00:12:37.040
But I overheard!

00:12:37.040 --> 00:12:38.410
Huh?

00:12:38.410 --> 00:12:41.080
We're going to disappear.

00:12:41.080 --> 00:12:43.040
Huh?!

00:12:43.040 --> 00:12:46.950
Mr. Seiji said it.

00:12:46.950 --> 00:12:50.120
It's fate for SPR5 to disappear!

00:12:54.250 --> 00:12:57.450
Yua-<i>tan</i>?! Yua-<i>tan</i>!

00:13:03.790 --> 00:13:05.870
Hey.

00:13:05.870 --> 00:13:10.370
If you could return to the past,
aren't there things you'd change?

00:13:10.370 --> 00:13:13.040
What are you asking all of a sudden?

00:13:13.040 --> 00:13:17.410
Everyone has a regret or two in their hearts.

00:13:21.200 --> 00:13:24.660
It's no use! No matter how many
times we try, we end up back here.

00:13:25.950 --> 00:13:28.080
--But, at this rate, didn't I tell you
we're going to be disbanded?!

00:13:28.080 --> 00:13:29.790
--I wonder why we always
come back to this moment?
--But, at this rate, didn't I tell you
we're going to be disbanded?!

00:13:29.790 --> 00:13:31.500
--I wonder why we always
come back to this moment?
--Yua!

00:13:31.500 --> 00:13:33.660
Dammit. They're so frustrating.

00:13:33.660 --> 00:13:35.950
Huh? Frustrating?

00:13:35.950 --> 00:13:39.830
They should just be honest and talk things out.

00:13:41.410 --> 00:13:42.870
I see.

00:13:42.870 --> 00:13:46.950
Since she wasn't able to do that, she...

00:13:46.950 --> 00:13:48.000
Takuya!

00:13:48.000 --> 00:13:49.080
Geek!

00:13:50.200 --> 00:13:52.000
Yua-<i>tan </i>said...!

00:13:53.450 --> 00:13:56.410
SPR5 is fated to disappear?

00:13:56.410 --> 00:13:58.620
It seems that was the producer's plan.

00:13:58.620 --> 00:14:01.950
That's why Yua-<i>tan </i>acted so recklessly...

00:14:01.950 --> 00:14:03.330
Isn't that weird?

00:14:03.330 --> 00:14:05.950
If they were going to be disbanded,
he'd just tell them so.

00:14:05.950 --> 00:14:08.450
It's the producer's decision, after all.

00:14:08.450 --> 00:14:09.700
Y-You think so?

00:14:09.700 --> 00:14:14.620
Fated to disappear... Lost? No way!

00:14:14.620 --> 00:14:16.290
What's the producer's name?!

00:14:16.290 --> 00:14:18.080
His pretty sure his name was Seiji.

00:14:18.080 --> 00:14:21.160
He's at the concert hall, right?
Let's go meet him.

00:14:21.160 --> 00:14:22.410
Wait, Takuya!

00:14:22.410 --> 00:14:26.080
We don't even know what he looks like!

00:14:26.080 --> 00:14:28.540
Hey, Geek.

00:14:28.540 --> 00:14:30.700
Tell me where Yua is.

00:14:35.250 --> 00:14:37.870
Nothing will change even if you sit there.

00:14:39.790 --> 00:14:40.700
Who are you?

00:14:40.700 --> 00:14:42.790
Let's go.

00:14:42.790 --> 00:14:43.950
What?

00:14:46.450 --> 00:14:49.370
You don't want to regret it, right?

00:14:50.660 --> 00:14:51.330
--Huh? W-Wait!

00:14:51.330 --> 00:14:53.790
--You don't want to regret it.
--Huh? W-Wait!

00:14:53.790 --> 00:14:55.790
Like me.

00:15:01.250 --> 00:15:02.660
I'm telling you to wait!

00:15:02.660 --> 00:15:06.580
Weren't you on the track team? You can run.

00:15:06.580 --> 00:15:10.540
Back then, I didn't have the courage.

00:15:10.540 --> 00:15:13.660
I was experimented on day after day.

00:15:13.660 --> 00:15:17.410
Before I realized it, I already
thought it was pointless to escape.

00:15:17.410 --> 00:15:19.160
Give it a rest, already!

00:15:22.200 --> 00:15:25.540
You have to go, or you'll regret it.

00:15:25.540 --> 00:15:30.370
I have to take you, or I'll regret it, too.

00:15:42.750 --> 00:15:46.700
Shit. Why isn't the producer here?

00:15:49.790 --> 00:15:52.540
It's impossible. I can't.

00:15:52.540 --> 00:15:55.370
I said terrible things.

00:15:55.370 --> 00:15:59.750
I did it for the team, but it all backfired.

00:15:59.750 --> 00:16:02.700
There's no place for me there anymore...

00:16:06.540 --> 00:16:08.000
You don't know that.

00:16:09.040 --> 00:16:10.330
Huh?

00:16:11.500 --> 00:16:13.120
Yua!

00:16:13.120 --> 00:16:15.750
We thought we heard your voice...

00:16:15.750 --> 00:16:17.750
We were so worried!

00:16:17.750 --> 00:16:23.290
Sorry. I'm sorry, everyone.

00:16:23.290 --> 00:16:25.620
It's fine. Let's talk things over later.

00:16:25.620 --> 00:16:27.870
We have to worry about the stage first.

00:16:27.870 --> 00:16:30.410
Come on, the fans are waiting.

00:16:31.620 --> 00:16:32.870
Yeah!

00:16:41.500 --> 00:16:42.950
Thank you.

00:16:45.120 --> 00:16:48.250
Thank goodness! Thank goodness!

00:16:49.660 --> 00:16:53.040
Yuki, I'm surprised you knew.

00:16:53.040 --> 00:16:55.830
The fact that Yua-<i>tan </i>was
part of the track team.

00:16:55.830 --> 00:16:59.620
That's pretty maniac trivia, even for the fans.

00:16:59.620 --> 00:17:02.580
I was a fan of Yua myself.

00:17:02.580 --> 00:17:06.250
Huh? Oh, I see! So that's what it was!

00:17:07.370 --> 00:17:09.700
You should do it today, Yua.

00:17:09.700 --> 00:17:10.870
Right.

00:17:10.870 --> 00:17:12.040
Huh?

00:17:14.660 --> 00:17:16.200
Then, let's do this!

00:17:16.200 --> 00:17:17.660
SPR5.

00:17:17.660 --> 00:17:20.790
Supreme Five!

00:17:23.620 --> 00:17:28.040
Aww, I wanted to see the concert!

00:17:32.580 --> 00:17:34.000
The sky...

00:17:38.500 --> 00:17:41.040
We're back?!

00:17:41.040 --> 00:17:42.830
Looks like it.

00:17:46.450 --> 00:17:47.700
That's right!

00:17:48.910 --> 00:17:52.620
I have to check if that was
really the past or not.

00:17:54.500 --> 00:17:55.080
Huh?

00:17:55.080 --> 00:17:56.620
"Yua did not make an appearance
do to a sudden illness."

00:17:58.330 --> 00:17:59.540
"The five members were involved
in Lost and currently missing."

00:17:59.540 --> 00:18:01.700
"The five members were involved
in Lost and currently missing."
Nothing changed...

00:18:03.040 --> 00:18:07.660
Yua-<i>tan </i>never made an appearance
and they were all caught up in Lost.

00:18:07.660 --> 00:18:14.660
No way... Then, what was all of that just now?

00:18:14.660 --> 00:18:18.370
Sorry. Go on ahead without me.

00:18:18.370 --> 00:18:19.660
Got it.

00:18:22.410 --> 00:18:27.660
If that wasn't the past, what was it?

00:18:27.660 --> 00:18:34.660
I think I understand now. What Tama-Shi is...

00:18:34.660 --> 00:18:35.700
Hm?

00:18:35.700 --> 00:18:41.500
That day, a lot people suddenly
got caught up in Lost.

00:18:41.500 --> 00:18:48.750
Their dreams and their treasured family.
Their unfinished will...

00:18:48.750 --> 00:18:54.410
I think Tama-shi is a person's
will that has taken shape.

00:18:54.410 --> 00:18:57.950
Just like how Akira tried to protect me.

00:18:57.950 --> 00:19:00.080
Then, what about Yua just now?

00:19:00.080 --> 00:19:03.500
Her regret was strong.

00:19:03.500 --> 00:19:08.410
I think that was a world her Tama-Shi created.

00:19:08.410 --> 00:19:10.700
What a rocky start...

00:19:10.700 --> 00:19:12.950
But I don't think it was pointless.

00:19:12.950 --> 00:19:15.580
Even though we couldn't change the past...

00:19:20.080 --> 00:19:24.910
This next song was the first song we
performed with our current members.

00:19:24.910 --> 00:19:28.410
No matter what comes our way,
the five of us will overcome it together.

00:19:28.410 --> 00:19:32.080
Our will and that promise
is the theme for this song.

00:19:32.080 --> 00:19:35.040
Though, I'm usually pulling all of them down.

00:19:35.040 --> 00:19:37.120
That's because you have the clumsy role, Rena.

00:19:37.120 --> 00:19:39.040
Don't call it a role!

00:19:39.040 --> 00:19:41.370
Then, what's my role?

00:19:41.370 --> 00:19:42.540
To be devious.

00:19:42.540 --> 00:19:43.580
Hey!

00:19:43.580 --> 00:19:47.330
We're like this, but please continue...

00:19:47.330 --> 00:19:49.580
...to support us!

00:19:50.700 --> 00:19:55.200
Now please listen to our song,
"With Your Breath!"

00:21:36.370 --> 00:21:38.330
What is it?

00:21:38.330 --> 00:21:40.160
Something's nearby.

00:21:42.370 --> 00:21:43.580
Tama-Shi?

00:21:43.580 --> 00:21:48.370
Leave it to me. Maybe I can
find out what it's thinking.

00:21:48.370 --> 00:21:52.370
Let me hear your will.

00:22:07.540 --> 00:22:08.870
Takuya!

00:22:08.870 --> 00:22:13.450
Will? What are you talking about, Sis?

00:22:14.950 --> 00:22:16.370
Souma?

00:22:17.790 --> 00:22:22.080
I missed you, Sis.

00:22:22.080 --> 00:22:25.290
What did you just do?

00:22:25.290 --> 00:22:29.000
What did I do? The same thing as you.

00:22:29.000 --> 00:22:31.160
Now, let's go home.

00:22:32.830 --> 00:22:38.040
What's wrong? Aren't you
happy that I'm still alive?

00:22:38.040 --> 00:22:39.410
Stop.

00:22:40.870 --> 00:22:42.290
Open your eyes!

00:22:42.290 --> 00:22:46.040
You're the one who needs to open your eyes, Sis.

00:22:46.040 --> 00:22:48.500
I see. It's him.

00:22:49.580 --> 00:22:51.080
Die.

00:22:54.200 --> 00:22:56.330
Stop!

00:22:56.330 --> 00:22:57.870
Stop, Souma!

00:22:57.870 --> 00:23:03.580
Let's go home. The two of us are family.

00:23:03.580 --> 00:23:07.410
Now that Dad is gone,
we have to support each other.

00:23:09.750 --> 00:23:12.950
Stop!

00:23:24.750 --> 00:23:26.790
These waves. It can't be...

00:23:36.950 --> 00:23:37.950
"AFTERLOST"

00:23:43.870 --> 00:23:46.160
Next Episode: "Suspicion."
